menu "ExecuTorch runtime (esp32 backend)"

config ET_PORTABLE_O2
    bool "Compile the ExecuTorch runtime and portable kernels at -O2 (default -Os)"
    default n
    help
        -Os keeps the image small; -O2 inlines and unrolls the runtime and
        the portable kernels a program registers, at the cost of code size.
        The story firmware cannot take it: its app grows by 160,528 B, past
        its partition, and its decode calls one portable kernel, twice a
        token (index_select); the custom ops and the fast paths run the rest
        (the backend's ESP32_BACKEND_OPS_O2). An A/B experiment switch for
        programs whose portable operators run on every inference.

endmenu
